  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (2250) and then preferring the lottery with the higher probability of exceeding this level. Lottery A has a 0.2% chance of exceeding 2250 (3000 > 2250), while Lottery B has only 0.1% (6000 > 2250), so the reason would favor A. However, the individual chose B and justified this by focusing on the higher maximum outcome (6000), treating probabilities as roughly equal due to their small size, and emphasizing the lack of downside. There is no mention or indication of computing an average outcome or evaluating outcomes relative to a derived reference point. The information considered (maximum gain, low probabilities, no loss) does not align with the aspiration level mechanism. The justification is based on maximax-like reasoning (choosing the highest possible outcome) rather than aspiration-level comparisons. Therefore, there is no evidence that the aspiration level reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
